From 90b311fcf2b4a9c7af0a0853d78f98be34301ec6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:21:18 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): "Pick for WCS" takes viewport picks in the default
 Model mode

The Setups page's WCS role draft leaves the toolbar's pick mode alone on
purpose (it takes faces, edges and corners together), but the viewport
sent a click to feature_click only in Face/Edge/Vertex mode. In the
default Model mode with no operation open, every click selected the whole
model and the draft never received a pick; the hover had the same gate.

interact::feature_routed now routes click and hover to the feature pick
rule while wcs_pick::collecting, whatever geo_pick is. Disarmed or paused,
the mode's own click behaviour is back. Apply is unchanged: the undoable
SetWcs, so a tilted frame is still placed and generation still refuses it
by name (#1518).

Pinned by wcs_pick_click_tests::an_armed_row_takes_viewport_picks_from_the_default_model_mode,
which arms the row from a fresh project and drives face, edge and corner
picks and the hover through interact::pick_at / update_hover.

Fixes #1562

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
